WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:04.290
Hi guys! Hi there!

2
00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:07.290
Sorry.

3
00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:17.290
You know what, tonight, based on our schedule, I'm not really going to have time to share a word this evening.

4
00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:24.290
So I thought I'm going to utilize the technology that we have and I'm going to send a short teaching video.

5
00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:26.290
Hallelujah!

6
00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:33.290
So I'll just trust that you're all good and will actually listen to it. In Jesus' name.

7
00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:38.290
Okay, so what's on my heart is the promises of God.

8
00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:49.290
You know, we're coming into the season of Christmas, we're preparing our songs and really last week I touched on it just slightly in the teaching.

9
00:00:50.290 --> 00:01:00.290
But God is really a God of promises. His word is full of promises and there is just something in the heart of God.

10
00:01:00.290 --> 00:01:16.290
What is amazing to me is that God, even through birthing Jesus, the Messiah, the King of kings, the glory one, the one full of glory, the one who is now, you know, got the name above every other name and is seated in the highest place in heaven.

11
00:01:17.290 --> 00:01:34.290
He was not afraid to begin in seed form. He was not afraid to put Jesus on the earth as a baby in a manger and to watch the process of the promise unfold.

12
00:01:35.290 --> 00:01:50.290
And I think we can all learn something so magnificent and so critical because whenever God speaks promises in your life, it's never going to come in its fullness when he speaks it.

13
00:01:51.290 --> 00:02:05.290
But it is going to come to its fullness if we will treasure it in our heart and we will walk with him and we will see the fullness of that word, that promise that he spoke come to pass in our lives.

14
00:02:05.290 --> 00:02:17.290
And I just want to look at it again from Luke. If you, you know, the story again of Luke or the, sorry, the story of Messiah being born, Jesus being born.

15
00:02:18.290 --> 00:02:32.290
If you look in Luke 1, when the angel answered, it says, talking to Mary, talking to Mary about this promise, this promise of the son of God going to come upon Mary through the Holy Spirit.

16
00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:41.290
Verse 35, the angel answered, the Holy Spirit will come on you, talking to Mary, and the power of the Most High will overshadow you.

17
00:02:42.290 --> 00:02:45.290
So the Holy One to be born will be called the Son of God.

18
00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:55.290
Even Elizabeth, your relative, is going to have a child in her old age and she, who was said to be unable to conceive, is in her sixth month.

19
00:02:56.290 --> 00:02:57.290
Another amazing promise.

20
00:02:58.290 --> 00:03:03.290
Verse 37, for no word, and that word for word there is rhema.

21
00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:14.290
Remember we talked, I taught a few weeks, no, months ago now, or a month and a bit ago, about the difference between a rhema and the logos word.

22
00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:17.290
Well, the word here in verse 37 is rhema.

23
00:03:17.290 --> 00:03:24.290
For no rhema word from God will ever fail, will never fail.

24
00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:32.290
And then Mary's response, which is just as important as the promise being spoken, which we can learn from.

25
00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:40.290
I am the Lord's servant, Mary answered, may it be to me according to your word.

26
00:03:41.290 --> 00:03:42.290
And then the angel left her.

27
00:03:42.290 --> 00:03:48.290
I find this an amazing teaching for us personally in our life with Christ.

28
00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:57.290
Because God is saying, no word that I speak over you will fail.

29
00:03:58.290 --> 00:04:01.290
No rhema, fresh spoken promise that I give to you.

30
00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:09.290
You know, if you're in a season where God is speaking a promise and it's quickened to your heart, whether it's through the written, the logos word, or He speaks it to you through,

31
00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:19.290
I don't know, someone, a prophet, or just in prayer, you hear Him speak about the next phase of your life and what He's going to be doing.

32
00:04:20.290 --> 00:04:37.290
God literally promises that if He speaks a rhema, fresh word, a promise, it will come that this whole meaning here in this part of the scripture is that no word spoken from the mouth of God that was formed in His mind,

33
00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:48.290
will ever come to you without also the strength and the ability to see it happen, to see it come to pass and fulfillment.

34
00:04:49.290 --> 00:04:55.290
So God says, I won't ever give you a promise and then leave it all up to you.

35
00:04:56.290 --> 00:05:16.290
He says, no, with that word that I speak comes with it, almost like in the word itself, spoken, spirit, will come strength and ability, obviously this is through the power of the Holy Spirit, comes to you also to see the fulfillment of that worked out in your life.

36
00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:43.290
Now I don't know if any of you feel like that, but have you not seen a promise come to pass where you've seen also this ability and strength as you've kept it in your heart, just like Mary did, it says later that Mary kept it in her heart, she treasured the word and she kept it close to her so that she would see it come to pass and she did see it come to pass.

37
00:05:43.290 --> 00:06:10.290
And so I just want to encourage you, first of all, what is maybe a new word or a new promise that God has been speaking to you of late, because if I talk for myself lately, I feel like in the last month or little while, God has been trying to open up my heart for a new season, a new word,

38
00:06:10.290 --> 00:06:19.290
because in my own life experience right now, I'm sort of already, I'm standing in the fulfillment of promises spoken about 10 years ago.

39
00:06:19.290 --> 00:06:38.290
I have a few specific words that I held on to that just spoke straight to my spirit even back then, that I actually am living in right now today, like the last year, the last two years, I feel like I'm living in the fulfillment of those promises from 10 years back that was spoken over my life.

40
00:06:38.290 --> 00:07:01.290
So it's like I treasured that, I walked with God, I walked through some hard seasons, walked through a journey of getting healed up on the inside from different things, and yet now I feel like because I'm standing in the fulfillment of promise, the Father is trying to get my attention and say, look, I've got some new things now to speak over your life.

41
00:07:02.290 --> 00:07:13.290
And it's like when something is born, when something is delivered, then it's like, okay, that word has come to its fulfillment.

42
00:07:13.290 --> 00:07:28.290
When Mary gave birth, she gave birth to the promise, and it came to pass, and then she needed an almost new word about how to raise this Son of God, this child that would be Messiah.

43
00:07:29.290 --> 00:07:32.290
So just a couple of thoughts, and I'll wrap it up.

44
00:07:33.290 --> 00:07:38.290
What is God the Father through the Spirit speaking to you?

45
00:07:38.290 --> 00:07:42.290
You know, we're coming also to the close of another year, the calendar year.

46
00:07:42.290 --> 00:07:48.290
I just want to encourage us to get in us a fresh word of God, a rhema word.

47
00:07:48.290 --> 00:07:49.290
Hold on to it.

48
00:07:49.290 --> 00:07:51.290
It might take 10 years to birth.

49
00:07:51.290 --> 00:07:52.290
It doesn't matter.

50
00:07:52.290 --> 00:08:05.290
There are some words God speaks, and they come to pass maybe in six months or a year, and there are some words that you have to treasure for a long time, even a decade before the fruit or the birth of that thing comes.

51
00:08:05.290 --> 00:08:08.290
But the point is, God is not afraid of the process.

52
00:08:08.290 --> 00:08:15.290
He's with you in it, and He gives, as it says, the strength, the ability to walk it out until it comes to pass.

53
00:08:15.290 --> 00:08:17.290
So what is God speaking in your heart?

54
00:08:17.290 --> 00:08:33.290
And if you don't know, if there's nothing that you say, yeah, this is already something I felt for a little time that God has been just through different means, maybe through teaching, maybe through something someone says over you, some encouragement you've had or through reading the Word.

55
00:08:33.290 --> 00:08:38.290
Usually, it'll come in multiple forms because God wants to get your attention.

56
00:08:39.290 --> 00:08:50.290
So I just want to open up your attention even to be switched on in this next little while for what the Father through the Spirit might be trying to get your attention into this next season.

57
00:08:50.290 --> 00:08:51.290
What is a new promise?

58
00:08:51.290 --> 00:08:54.290
What's a new freshly spoken word of God in your life?

59
00:08:55.290 --> 00:09:05.290
And then, secondly, I want you to already think about what you're standing in that has come from as the result of words already spoken over your life.

60
00:09:05.290 --> 00:09:07.290
Because then you can give thanks to God.

61
00:09:07.290 --> 00:09:12.290
En dankzegging is ook, we worden geroepen om te bidden.

62
00:09:12.290 --> 00:09:16.290
En het Woord zegt dat we in elke situatie dank moeten geven.

63
00:09:16.290 --> 00:09:20.290
We moeten eigenlijk in alle dingen, altijd dank geven.

64
00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:25.290
Dus ik wil dat we overwegen wat God spreekt en wat Hij al gedaan heeft.

65
00:09:25.290 --> 00:09:33.290
In wat leef je als de vervulling van een woord dat Hij in het verleden sprak waar je daadwerkelijk in staat?

66
00:09:33.290 --> 00:09:40.290
Misschien heb je er nog niet zo over nagedacht, maar je staat eigenlijk al in de belofte, de vervulling van een woord dat al over je leven gesproken is.

67
00:09:40.290 --> 00:09:45.290
En begin dan God te danken, wees opzettelijk in het danken van Hem.

68
00:09:45.290 --> 00:09:48.290
Man, ik heb je dit met mij zien uitwerken.

69
00:09:48.290 --> 00:09:55.290
Ik heb je me de kracht en het vermogen door de Geest zien geven om dit tot stand te brengen.

70
00:09:55.290 --> 00:09:59.290
En geef God lof en geef God dank in Jezus' naam.

71
00:09:59.290 --> 00:10:00.290
Amen.

72
00:10:00.290 --> 00:10:02.290
Ik zie je vanavond.

73
00:10:02.290 --> 00:10:05.290
En ik ben enthousiast.

74
00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:06.290
Oké.

75
00:10:06.290 --> 00:10:07.290
Hou van jullie, jongens.
